  "notes": "A する-verb from {履行|りこう}, a compound of {履|り} (carry out, step on) and {行|こう} (perform, go). A formal word most often found in legal, contractual, and official contexts. Not typically used in casual conversation.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive — takes を to mark the obligation being fulfilled.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {契約|けいやく}を{履行|りこう}する — to fulfill a contract\n- {義務|ぎむ}を{履行|りこう}する — to perform a duty\n- {債務|さいむ}{履行|りこう} — performance of debt obligations\n- {履行|りこう}{期限|きげん} — deadline for performance\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {遂行|すいこう}する — to accomplish, to execute (focuses on carrying through to completion)\n- {実行|じっこう}する — to execute, to carry out (more general, less formal)\n- {果|は}たす — to fulfill, to accomplish (native Japanese, usable in casual contexts)",
